  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-27 at dev f474411e11. STILL VIOLATED, unchanged: objc.yaml:214-222 NSTask [launch, launchAndReturnError:, waitUntilExit, terminate, interrupt] and swift.yaml:152-159 Process [launchPath, waitUntilExit, terminate, interrupt], both under subprocess, both notes unchanged. python.yaml:693-695 (kill/terminate ipc_send, WI-dupok) and rust.yaml:431-436 (Child.kill ipc_send) unchanged.\n\nShipped CLI (io-boundaries):\n  objc [task terminate] / [task interrupt] / [task waitUntilExit] -> subprocess NSTask.{terminate,interrupt,waitUntilExit}\n  swift p.terminate() / p.interrupt() / p.waitUntilExit()         -> subprocess Process.{terminate,interrupt,waitUntilExit}\n\nA WORSE DEFECT IN THE SAME SWIFT ROW, found while reproducing this one and filed separately (missed boundaries, the false-all-clear direction): the swift row catalogues NO launch. p.run(), t.launch(), Process.run(url, arguments:) and Process.launchedProcess(launchPath:arguments:) all produce 0 chains, while every non-launch member above is reported as subprocess. The row's one launch-sounding entry, launchPath, is a property, never a call. objc lacks the class-method launcher launchedTaskWithLaunchPath:arguments: the same way. See the item filed today."  # a3ca
